const pages = [
  ['platform-choice','switch-vs-switch-2','comparison','Switch vs Switch 2 for Echoes of Teradea','Both Nintendo systems launch on September 24, 2026 and both have confirmed physical preorders. Choose by the console you own and the exact retail variant; Natsume has not published a technical comparison or upgrade path.',['The publisher lists Nintendo Switch and Nintendo Switch 2 as separate launch platforms.','The Natsume Store offers separate physical selections for both systems at the reviewed price.','No official source currently states resolution, frame rate, load-time, save-transfer, cross-buy, or paid-upgrade differences.'],'This comparison prevents a platform logo from being mistaken for a performance promise. It is most useful before placing a physical preorder.',['Confirm the selected box version at checkout.','Treat performance claims as unverified until official store specifications appear.','Recheck save transfer and upgrade rules before launch.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['platform-choice','switch-2-vs-ps5','comparison','Switch 2 vs PS5 for Echoes of Teradea','Switch 2 and PS5 are both confirmed launch and physical-preorder platforms. Current first-party material does not establish which version performs better, so the safe decision is based on hardware ownership, play location, retailer terms, and later technical listings.',['Both versions are scheduled for the same September 24 date.','Both appear in the Natsume Store physical selector and may qualify for the live store offer.','Natsume has not published resolution, frame rate, loading, controller-feature, or content-parity tables.'],'Use this page to distinguish verified availability from an unsupported “best version” ranking.',['Compare live price and delivery estimates.','Wait for official platform listings before judging technical performance.','Verify bonus wording for the exact selected product.'],'preorder,store'],
  ['platform-choice','ps5-vs-xbox-series-xs','comparison','PS5 vs Xbox Series X|S for Echoes of Teradea','Both consoles are confirmed for launch, but only PS5 is currently named in Natsume’s physical preorder program. Xbox remains a confirmed game platform, not a confirmed boxed edition in the cited sources.',['The March, May, and June announcements include PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.','The Natsume Store selector lists PS5 but does not list an Xbox physical variant.','Absence from the current physical selector does not prove that Xbox will never receive retail stock.'],'This page answers the edition-availability difference without inventing a performance difference.',['Choose PS5 if the current physical offer is essential.','Wait for an official Xbox storefront for digital price and download details.','Do not assume cross-save or feature parity beyond confirmed core content.'],'preorder,store'],
  ['platform-choice','steam-vs-console','comparison','Steam vs Console for Echoes of Teradea','Steam, Switch 2, Switch, PS5, and Xbox Series X|S share the confirmed launch date. Steam is the confirmed PC route, while current physical preorders are limited to Switch 2, Switch, and PS5.',['PC is explicitly identified as Steam in Natsume announcements.','No PC system requirements, Steam Deck status, input details, or download size are published in the cited sources.','Console announcement does not prove physical stock; the current physical program names three platforms.'],'Use this comparison to decide between a physical-copy priority and waiting for PC specifications.',['Wishlist or verify the official Steam listing when available.','Do not borrow requirements from earlier Harvest Moon titles.','Compare digital policies only after official platform pages publish them.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['platform-choice','physical-vs-digital','comparison','Physical vs Digital Echoes of Teradea Editions','A physical preorder is currently verifiable for Switch 2, Switch, and PS5. Digital versions are implied by the five-platform launch, but official digital prices, preload timing, file sizes, and bonuses remain unpublished.',['The first-party store lists boxed variants at $49.99 as reviewed.','Xbox Series X|S and Steam are launch platforms without current physical variants in the cited offer.','The Lupo plush is merchandise tied to qualifying preorder language, not a confirmed digital bonus.'],'This page helps buyers avoid treating a physical-store offer as proof of digital terms.',['Choose physical when ownership format and the live bonus matter.','Wait for platform storefronts before comparing digital prices.','Check cancellation and delivery exposure before ordering.'],'preorder,store'],
  ['platform-choice','same-day-platform-launch','matrix','Same-Day Platform Launch Matrix','Natsume schedules all five platform families for September 24, 2026: Switch 2, Switch, PS5, Xbox Series X|S, and Steam. Exact regional unlock hours are not yet part of that confirmation.',['The May and June releases repeat one launch date across the platform list.','A shared calendar date does not establish simultaneous global unlock time.','Physical delivery can differ from digital availability because store shipping is not guaranteed for release day.'],'Use the matrix for release planning while keeping time-zone and delivery questions separate.',['Record the confirmed date.','Check the relevant platform store for local unlock time.','Treat retailer arrival estimates as logistics, not release-date changes.'],'preorder,trailer'],
  ['platform-choice','single-player-platform-choice','guide','Single-Player Platform Choice Guide','The Natsume Store classifies Echoes of Teradea as a one-player game. Platform choice therefore centers on hardware, format, portability, and later technical specifications—not multiplayer population.',['The live product page says “Players: 1 Player.”','No co-op, cross-play, or online multiplayer system is announced.','Single-player status does not answer cloud-save, achievements, controller, or performance questions.'],'This guide redirects the buying decision toward confirmed differences instead of imaginary multiplayer considerations.',['Choose the device and format that fit your routine.','Wait for official save and technical details.','Do not purchase on the assumption that co-op will be added.'],'store'],
  ['platform-choice','platform-facts-vs-assumptions','matrix','Platform Facts vs Assumptions','Confirmed platform facts are the five launch families, shared date, one-player classification, and three current physical variants. Performance, cross-save, cross-buy, upgrade paths, file size, and preload remain assumptions until official listings say otherwise.',['Release announcements establish availability, not every technical feature.','A trailer can show gameplay without proving final platform performance.','Retailer metadata can change and should be rechecked before purchase.'],'Use this page as a compact evidence filter when comparing rumors or store snippets.',['Match each claim to a first-party source.','Separate physical availability from launch availability.','Leave missing technical fields blank instead of estimating.'],'announcement,trailer,store'],

  ['system-workflows','animal-obstacle-workflow','workflow','Animal Companion Obstacle Workflow','Confirmed animal abilities support a clear exploration loop: identify a blocked route, select a companion suited to movement or destruction, pass the obstacle, and search the newly reachable area for treasure or other discoveries.',['Natsume says animals can help leap across terrain and destroy rocks or fallen trees.','Companions are functional exploration partners rather than cosmetic followers only.','Specific animal-to-ability assignments and unlock requirements are not yet published.'],'This workflow gives the companion database a durable structure for launch-day observations.',['Record the obstacle type.','Test which verified companion solves it.','Link the unlocked area to its treasure, resource, or destination page.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['system-workflows','hidden-area-discovery-loop','workflow','Hidden Area Discovery Loop','Hidden-area discovery combines player movement, animal traversal abilities, obstacle removal, and careful route observation. The confirmed systems support the loop even though exact locations are not public.',['Players can jump, climb ladders, and scale vines.','Animals can reach hidden areas and break environmental obstacles.','The world includes caves, islands, wilderness, treasures, and rare collectibles.'],'Use this page to plan a post-launch map method without publishing invented coordinates now.',['Mark the visible barrier and nearby landmark.','Separate player-movement access from companion-required access.','Verify the reward and return route before publishing.'],'announcement,preorder'],
  ['system-workflows','camp-to-merchant-workflow','workflow','Campsite to Traveling Merchant Workflow','Campsites support rest, stamina recovery, and cooking during long trips, while traveling merchants offer goods unavailable elsewhere. Together they form a travel-resupply workflow, though schedules and locations are not yet confirmed.',['The world is described as too large to explore in one in-game day.','Camping extends expeditions through rest and cooking.','Traveling merchants are associated with exclusive items.'],'This workflow separates the confirmed system relationship from unverified rotations or inventories.',['Reach or use a verified campsite.','Check nearby travel routes for a merchant encounter.','Record item, price, day, weather, and repeatability after launch.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['system-workflows','camp-stamina-cooking-loop','workflow','Camp, Stamina, and Cooking Loop','During extended exploration, campsites let players rest, recover stamina, and cook by the fire. The practical loop is travel, monitor stamina, camp before exhaustion, prepare food, and continue the expedition.',['Camping is explicitly tied to long-distance exploration.','Rest and food both belong to the campsite description.','No recovery values, recipe list, placement rules, or time cost are officially published.'],'This page provides a useful planning sequence without pretending to be a completed recipe or campsite database.',['Carry verified cooking materials after launch.','Use stamina thresholds only when measured.','Record whether rest advances time and how much it restores.'],'preorder,store'],
  ['system-workflows','nautical-chart-island-loop','workflow','Nautical Chart to Remote Island Workflow','Nautical charts lead to remote islands, where players can hunt treasure and encounter rare animals not found on the mainland. That creates a chart, travel, search, befriend, and return loop.',['Remote islands are a confirmed exploration destination.','Rare island animals can be befriended.','Chart sources, island names, transport mechanics, and weather restrictions remain unpublished.'],'This workflow defines which evidence belongs on future island pages.',['Verify the chart source and destination.','Document the departure method and prerequisites.','Separate treasures, collectibles, animals, and return conditions.'],'announcement,preorder'],
  ['system-workflows','cave-ore-gem-loop','workflow','Cave, Ore, and Gem Expedition Loop','Maze-like caves contain ore and gems, making cave exploration a distinct resource expedition. A reliable loop will connect route entry, stamina preparation, navigation, extraction, inventory choices, and safe return.',['Caves are described as maze-like rather than simple resource rooms.','Ore and gems are named cave rewards.','Exact mine floors, tool levels, spawn tables, and hazards are not yet confirmed.'],'This page gives mining data a structure that can be filled with reproducible observations after launch.',['Record entrance and prerequisites.','Map branches without assuming random generation.','Log verified resources and the conditions under which they appear.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['system-workflows','power-wisp-progression-loop','workflow','Power Wisp Progression Loop','The confirmed progression chain is to solve Power Statue puzzles, release dormant Power Wisps, receive Power Wisp Fruits, and trade those fruits at the Forest Goddess Statue for stamina increases and useful abilities.',['Power Statues are puzzle-linked progression objects.','Power Wisp Fruits connect rescue activity to character growth.','Costs, ability names, puzzle solutions, and statue locations are not published.'],'This page preserves the complete official chain instead of splitting each unknown value into a thin placeholder.',['Find and verify a statue.','Document the puzzle and released Wisp.','Record the fruit reward and confirmed exchange result.'],'announcement'],
  ['system-workflows','happilia-restoration-loop','workflow','Happilia and Village Restoration Loop','Helping villagers and contributing to Teradea’s development generates Happilia. That places community assistance inside the wider goal of reviving villages and restoring the land.',['Happilia is explicitly earned by helping people and developing Teradea.','The story names four villages connected to the restoration journey.','No point values, thresholds, shop unlocks, or restoration costs are published.'],'This workflow distinguishes the confirmed social-development link from assumed reputation mechanics.',['Identify the verified helping action.','Record the Happilia result after launch.','Connect confirmed milestones to the affected village page.'],'announcement,preorder'],
  ['system-workflows','farm-to-expedition-planning','workflow','Farm to Expedition Planning Loop','Echoes of Teradea combines running a farm with journeys through villages, caves, wilderness, and islands. The planning loop is to prepare at the farm, choose a goal and companion, travel, gather or help, then return with verified resources and progress.',['Building and running a farm is a core confirmed activity.','Exploration can extend beyond one in-game day and includes wilderness risk.','Exact inventory limits, shipping rules, crop cycles, and farm upgrades remain unknown.'],'This page explains how the two headline pillars connect without inventing farming data.',['Set one expedition objective.','Prepare only with confirmed items and abilities.','Log what returns to the farm and what advances restoration.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['system-workflows','wildlife-risk-recovery-loop','workflow','Wildlife Risk and Recovery Loop','Dangerous wild animals appear at night and can catch the player. Natsume says the penalty can include losing collected items and being returned to the farm, so route planning should account for time, escape, and carried value.',['Night wolves are part of Bloomfield’s opening threat.','The wilderness includes bears, tigers, and other dangerous animals.','Combat, stealth, taming conditions, exact loss rules, and difficulty settings are not fully described.'],'This workflow creates a place to publish tested risk rules later without presenting guesses as survival advice.',['Track time and the nearby safe route.','Record the animal and encounter trigger.','Verify which items are lost and where recovery begins.'],'announcement'],
  ['system-workflows','treasure-collectible-planning','workflow','Treasure and Rare Collectible Planning','Treasures, rare collectibles, caves, islands, animal abilities, and obstacle removal form a discovery network. A useful hunt starts with a verified access requirement and ends with a reproducible location and reward.',['The open world contains treasures and rare collectibles.','Animal abilities can reveal or reach hidden areas.','Official materials do not provide a treasure count, checklist, coordinates, or reward table.'],'This page defines a quality standard for future collectible entries and avoids publishing empty item names.',['State the access prerequisite.','Anchor the location to a stable landmark.','Verify the collected object and whether it respawns.'],'announcement,store'],
  ['system-workflows','village-travel-priority-loop','matrix','Four-Village Travel Priority Framework','Bloomfield is the player’s home, Tidewind faces storms, Quarrytop faces earthquakes, and Maplehill needs renewed community life. The game’s exact quest order is unknown, so the safest framework organizes travel by confirmed village purpose rather than claiming a route.',['Four named settlements anchor the restoration story.','Each published village has a different narrative or economic role.','Unlock order, fast travel, road layout, and mandatory sequence are not confirmed.'],'Use this framework as a spoiler-light orientation page until verified quest dependencies exist.',['Start from the confirmed home context.','Choose the village tied to the current verified objective.','Update order only after reproducible progression data exists.'],'announcement,preorder'],

  ['world-connections','bloomfield-wolves-connection','dossier','Bloomfield, Night Wolves, and the Opening Threat','Bloomfield Village is the protagonist’s home, and the spreading Forest of Echoes mist brings wild wolves out at night. That connection establishes the local threat that starts the wider journey.',['The protagonist was raised in Bloomfield Village.','Wolves appear outside the village under cover of night.','A large guardian wolf is rumored, but its exact identity and relationship to Lupo are not confirmed.'],'This dossier keeps the opening premise distinct from later village disasters and from merchandise descriptions.',['Use Bloomfield as the home anchor.','Treat ordinary wolves and the rumored guardian separately.','Add quest steps only after official or verified gameplay evidence.'],'announcement'],
  ['world-connections','forest-mist-guardian-spirits','dossier','Forest Mist and Guardian Spirits Connection','The mist spreading from the Forest of Echoes threatens Teradea, while helping Guardian Spirits revive the land becomes the larger mission. The official premise connects the forest mystery to supernatural restoration without revealing the resolution.',['The Forest of Echoes is the named origin of the mist.','Guardian Spirits are allies in reviving and revitalizing Teradea.','The cause of the mist, number of spirits, powers, and ending remain unrevealed.'],'This page explains the central narrative connection without inventing lore or spoilers.',['Keep cause and effect separate until confirmed.','Record each named spirit only from a primary source.','Attach future discoveries to the relevant village or forest event.'],'announcement,preorder'],
  ['world-connections','tidewind-storm-restoration','dossier','Tidewind Storm and Restoration Connection','Tidewind is the port village where the player investigates violent storms. Its disaster gives the restoration journey a coastal and weather-focused branch.',['Tidewind is explicitly described as a port village.','The player travels there to uncover what causes the storms.','The source does not name the culprit, damaged facilities, quest chain, or repair materials.'],'Use this dossier to group verified Tidewind characters, services, weather events, and quests when they are revealed.',['Separate the storm mystery from normal weather.','Verify every location within Tidewind.','Do not infer fishing, shipping, or boat systems solely from “port village.”'],'announcement'],
  ['world-connections','quarrytop-earthquake-mining','dossier','Quarrytop Earthquake and Mining Connection','Quarrytop is a mining village affected by earthquakes. The setting links a community disaster to the broader cave and ore landscape, but Natsume has not said that mining causes the earthquakes.',['Quarrytop’s mining identity and earthquake problem are both confirmed.','The player goes there to investigate the mystery.','Causation, mine layout, damaged buildings, bosses, and repair sequence remain unknown.'],'This dossier prevents an intuitive but unsupported causal claim from becoming site lore.',['Document the village and mine as separate places until verified.','Record earthquake triggers and consequences.','Add resource data only from repeatable gameplay.'],'announcement'],
  ['world-connections','maplehill-community-revival','dossier','Maplehill Community Revival Connection','Maplehill is a once-thriving town and cultural center whose light and community must be revived. Its branch emphasizes social and cultural restoration rather than a named storm or earthquake.',['Maplehill is one of four confirmed settlements.','Its published problem is fading light and community life.','The source does not identify a single disaster, festival schedule, mayor, shops, or restoration requirements.'],'This dossier preserves Maplehill’s distinct narrative purpose while waiting for concrete local data.',['Track cultural locations and residents separately.','Connect verified helping actions to Happilia only when observed.','Avoid inventing a festival calendar from the “cultural center” label.'],'announcement'],
  ['world-connections','guardian-wolf-vs-lupo','comparison','Guardian Wolf vs Lupo: What Is Actually Confirmed?','Official material mentions a rumored large guardian wolf and separately identifies Lupo as a baby wolf plush called the Bloomfield Guardian. The sources do not confirm that they are the same character or define an in-game relationship.',['The guardian wolf belongs to the opening mystery.','Lupo is named in preorder merchandise language.','Merchandise wording is not proof of an in-game identity, ability, or quest role.'],'This comparison prevents two similar wolf references from being merged into a false character fact.',['Keep both records separate.','Update only when a trailer, profile, or gameplay scene connects them.','Do not call the plush DLC or an in-game pet.'],'announcement,preorder,store'],
  ['world-connections','four-village-disaster-map','matrix','Four-Village Disaster and Restoration Map','The confirmed world map of story purposes is: Bloomfield as home under the forest mist and wolf threat, Tidewind under storms, Quarrytop under earthquakes, and Maplehill in cultural decline.',['All four places are named in the original announcement.','Each settlement supports a different restoration question.','Distances, borders, travel order, and complete disaster chronology are not public.'],'This is a conceptual map for navigation, not a claim about geographic coordinates.',['Use the settlement names as hubs.','Attach only verified threats and goals.','Replace conceptual links with measured routes after launch.'],'announcement'],
  ['world-connections','friendship-romance-restoration','dossier','Friendship, Romance, and Restoration Connection','Building friendships and choosing among ten love interests are confirmed life-sim systems, while helping villagers contributes to Teradea’s development. Official sources connect social play to the world but do not publish romance statistics or restoration bonuses.',['There are five bachelors and five bachelorettes.','Players can form bonds, experience relationship events, and choose a partner.','Candidate names, birthdays, gifts, schedules, heart thresholds, and same-gender options are not confirmed in the cited text.'],'This page holds the verified social-system relationship without generating empty gift or event pages.',['Create candidate pages only when identity is verified.','Record relationship events from repeatable play.','Keep Happilia gains separate from romance unless the game explicitly links them.'],'announcement,store'],

  ['preorder-decisions','lupo-bonus-verification','checklist','How to Verify the Lupo Plush Bonus','A qualifying listing must explicitly show the Lupo baby wolf plush offer for the selected product and platform. Because the bonus is while supplies last, an old announcement alone is not enough at checkout.',['Natsume introduced Lupo with the preorder campaign.','The first-party store calls the plush an exclusive offer.','The bonus is physical merchandise, not confirmed DLC or an in-game item.'],'Use this checklist immediately before payment and retain the order confirmation.',['Check the live product title or bonus text.','Confirm the exact platform variant.','Save evidence of eligibility and review delivery terms.'],'preorder,store'],
  ['preorder-decisions','retailer-platform-checklist','checklist','Retailer and Platform Preorder Checklist','Natsume has named its store, Amazon, Target, Walmart, Best Buy, and GameStop, but a named retailer does not guarantee every platform, permanent stock, or identical bonus terms.',['Amazon was named with Switch 2, Switch, and PS5 when preorders opened.','Later material named additional major retailers.','Live seller identity, stock, pickup, cancellation, and bonus wording can differ.'],'This page turns the retailer list into a purchase verification process.',['Confirm seller and platform.','Compare bonus and cancellation language.','Record delivery or pickup estimate before paying.'],'preorder,trailer,store'],
  ['preorder-decisions','price-tax-shipping-checklist','checklist','Price, Tax, Duty, and Shipping Checklist','The reviewed Natsume Store price starts at $49.99, but the checkout total can also include tax, shipping, customs, or duties depending on destination.',['The headline product price is not a universal regional price.','International buyers are responsible for compatibility and import exposure under the displayed policy.','A mixed preorder and in-stock order may be held until all items are available.'],'Use this checklist to compare real delivered cost rather than headline price alone.',['Select the correct variant.','Calculate checkout shipping and tax.','Estimate import charges and verify the address.'],'store'],
  ['preorder-decisions','release-day-delivery-expectations','guide','Release-Day Delivery Expectations','September 24, 2026 is the game’s release date, but the Natsume Store does not guarantee that a physical preorder arrives that day. Release timing and parcel delivery are separate events.',['The store says most preorders ship a few days before release.','Carrier transit is unpredictable and release-day delivery is not guaranteed.','Digital unlock timing is also still unpublished.'],'This guide prevents a shipping delay from being mistaken for a release-date change.',['Use the confirmed date for the game.','Use tracking for the parcel.','Check a platform storefront separately for digital availability.'],'preorder,store'],
  ['preorder-decisions','combined-order-shipping-risk','guide','Combined Preorder Shipping Risk','The Natsume Store says orders containing preorder and in-stock items are held until all items are available. Buyers who want an in-stock item sooner should place it separately.',['Combined-order handling is a store logistics rule.','It can delay the in-stock item even when the game remains on schedule.','Address changes and cancellation limits follow the live store policy.'],'This page answers a concrete ordering risk that the general game release page cannot.',['Separate time-sensitive in-stock goods.','Verify address before checkout.','Read current cancellation and support terms.'],'store']
];

